  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bridging the gap - integrating migrants</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project enhances labour migration governance in Malta through private sector engagement, capacity building of employers and targeted integration measures for Third Country Nationals. The action seeks to contribute to the promotion of migrant workers&apos; rights and integration and leverages on different components such as stakeholder engagement, development of strategic partnerships in Malta, creation of a space for discussion and networking around labour migration, promotion of sustainable standards for workers in the logistics industry, in particular ride-hailing and food delivery sector, capacity building and training for fair and ethical recruitment and employment and improved work conditions. The proposed response enhances the capacity of Bolt in Malta and internationally, providing tools to align to ethical and fair recruitment standards and to counter labour exploitation. By providing capacity building and trainings to fleets and couriers and drivers in the ride-hailing and food delivery sector the project contributes to uphold worker&apos;s rights, improved working conditions a more reliable and motivated workforce. Ultimately, by creating a space for discussion on labour mobility, it is expected that the project will benefit the labour market in Malta and contribute to create a more inclusive society.</narrative>
  </description>
